# Shell scripts must stay LF-only. A CRLF sneaking into the shebang line makes the
# kernel look for an interpreter named "/bin/sh\r", which fails with a confusing
# "no such file or directory" on the VPS. These scripts ship code to production and
# guard the network boundary, so a silent line-ending break is not acceptable.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The pinned exact-match config the vet job and adapter read; keep it LF so a
# checkout on Linux is byte-identical to what tests assert against.
*.mjs text eol=lf
